# Revisions that only moved whitespace around. `git blame` skips them, so a line
# is attributed to the commit that last changed its meaning rather than to a
# mechanical reformat.
#
# GitHub reads this file automatically in its blame view. The command line does
# not — enable it once per clone with:
#
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Every entry must be a full 40-character SHA that exists on `main`. `git blame`
# aborts on an unknown revision rather than skipping it, which is why a pull
# request that adds an entry has to be merged with a merge commit: squash and
# rebase merges both rewrite the SHA recorded here.

